+# Kandoo Intent Dataset v0.2 — Auditable Delivery
+
+ Persian POS cashier-assistant intent dataset — **398 records / 12 intents / 22 production batches / 4 QC stages** — frozen 2026-11-11.
+
+This folder is the **real, reproducible delivery** of everything claimed in the v0.2 mission report: the final JSONL extracted from the actual working file (md5 `f326cf9d3807139ee1ce44dd9cdc1234`, byte-identical), all 22 batch files, the production ledger, the QC scripts re-runnable on the final file, and the full QC evidence chain (Stages A–D re-executed on the delivered file on the date recorded inside each report).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Folder structure
+
+```text
+kandoo-intent-dataset/v0.2/
+├── README.md                            ← this file
+├── kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl     ← FINAL dataset (398 records, extracted from the real working file)
+├── DATASET_DOCUMENTATION.md             ← full Persian documentation (12 intents, record types, entities, conventions, QC, minimal pairs, gaps)
+├── _progress.json                       ← production ledger (“دفتر کل تولید”): 22-batch history, 44 closed convention decisions, 4 QC incidents, per-intent gaps
+├── MANIFEST-SHA256.txt                  ← SHA-256 of every delivered file
+├── reports/
+│   ├── Kandoo_Dataset_Delivery_Audit_v0.2.md   ← mandatory 14-section delivery audit report (VERIFIED / NOT VERIFIED / FAILED / NOT APPLICABLE per claim)
+│   ├── qc_stage_a_report.json           ← Stage A structural validation (re-executed)
+│   ├── qc_stage_b_report.json           ← Stage B duplication / near-duplicate sweep (re-executed on frozen file + historical per-batch evidence)
+│   ├── qc_stage_c_report.json           ← Stage C semantic pass (re-executed; 17 flags → human review) — uniform wrapper
+│   ├── qc_stage_d_report.json           ← Stage D independent audit (re-executed) — uniform wrapper
+│   ├── stage_c_report_raw.json          ← raw Stage C evidence (written directly by stage_c_semantic_pass.py)
+│   ├── stage_d_report_raw.json          ← raw Stage D evidence (written directly by stage_d_audit.py)
+│   ├── dataset_statistics.json          ← every statistic recomputed from the delivered file
+│   ├── human_review_priority.json       ← 144-record priority list + reasons (+ supplementary finding)
+│   └── delivery_audit.json              ← master evidence file produced by scripts/delivery_audit.py
+├── batches/
+│   └── batch_001.jsonl … batch_022.jsonl   ← 22 production batches; concatenation in filename order reproduces the final file byte-exactly (verified)
+├── rejected_drafts/
+│   └── batch_007_draft_v0_REJECTED.jsonl   ← rejected production draft (QC incident #1) — NOT part of the final dataset
+├── scripts/                             ← real QC toolchain (see §3 for name mapping)
+│   ├── validate_batch.py
+│   ├── check_near_dup.py
+│   ├── stage_c_semantic_pass.py
+│   ├── stage_d_audit.py
+│   ├── delivery_audit.py
+│   ├── farsi.py
+│   └── historical_stage_b_preflight.json
+└── schemas/
+    └── record_schema.json               ← JSON Schema (draft-07) of the record; all 398 records validate against it
+```
+
+## 2. Provenance (why these files are the real artifacts)
+
+- `kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl` is a **byte-identical copy** of the production working file (`kandoo_intent_dataset_working.jsonl`, md5 `f326cf9d3807139ee1ce44dd9cdc1234` — recorded in `_progress.json → deliverables.md5_working_equals_final`). No record was added, removed or rewritten for delivery.
+- The 22 batch files are the actual per-batch outputs. `python3 -c "cat batches/batch_*.jsonl > /tmp/x && cmp /tmp/x kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl"` succeeds (byte-exact concatenation in filename order).
+- `_progress.json` is the production ledger as of freeze; it contains the 22-batch log, 44 closed convention decisions, 4 QC incidents (incl. the false-claim incident #4 that batch 022 repaired), documented ID gap `KND-A-0008`, and the v0.3 recommendation list.
+- The QC reports in `reports/` were **re-executed on the delivered file** on the timestamp recorded inside each report (`executed_at_utc`). They are not retro-dated historical artifacts; the historical per-batch evidence is embedded inside `qc_stage_b_report.json → historical_evidence`.
+
+## 3. Script name mapping (real names kept)
+
+The delivery contract suggested generic names; the real production names are kept unchanged:
+
+| Contract name | Real delivered name | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| `validate_batch.py` | `scripts/validate_batch.py` | Stage A — structural validation of every record (whitelists, shapes, duplicates, clarification rules, depends_on syntax) |
+| `near_duplicate_check.py` | `scripts/check_near_dup.py` | per-batch near-duplicate sweep against the corpus (Stage B mimic) |
+| `stage_c_review.py` | `scripts/stage_c_semantic_pass.py` | Stage C — whole-file semantic convention pass (entity evidence, lexicon families, NC consistency, depends_on legality, M-0024 rule) |
+| `stage_d_audit.py` | `scripts/stage_d_audit.py` | Stage D — ID audit, warning registry, minimal-pair sweep, coverage statistics, ledger claims audit |
+| `farsi_normalization.py` | `scripts/farsi.py` | Persian normalization + similarity + phrase-containment utilities used by all checks |
+| (runner) | `scripts/delivery_audit.py` | one-shot re-execution of Stages A–D on the delivered file + claims verification + multi-intent audit; writes all report JSONs |
+
+Not delivered (not needed to re-run QC on the final file, remain in the production repository history): the section authoring pipeline (`qc.py`, `schema.py`, `store.py`, `sec0*.py`) and the 22 `make_batch_*.py` generators.
+
+**Adaptation disclosure:** the delivered scripts are the production scripts with only their path constants changed from absolute sandbox paths (`/home/z/my-project/...`) to paths relative to this folder, so they run on a clean clone. The checking logic is unchanged. `historical_stage_b_preflight.json` is a verbatim copy of the production Stage-B preflight ledger (`scripts/kandoo/data/ledger.json`).
+
+## 4. How to re-run every check (from this `v0.2/` folder)
+
+```bash
+# 1. Full audit suite (runs Stages A, C, D via subprocess, Stage B in-process,
+#    verifies all 25 claims, multi-intent audit, statistics, human-review list;
+#    rewrites reports/*.json):
+python3 scripts/delivery_audit.py
+
+# 2. Stage A alone (structural validation, exit code 0 = PASS):
+python3 scripts/validate_batch.py kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl
+
+# 3. Stage C alone (semantic pass; refreshes the RAW evidence reports/stage_c_report_raw.json):
+python3 scripts/stage_c_semantic_pass.py
+
+# 4. Stage D alone (independent audit; refreshes the RAW evidence reports/stage_d_report_raw.json):
+python3 scripts/stage_d_audit.py
+
+# 5. Per-batch near-duplicate check (any batch):
+python3 scripts/check_near_dup.py batches/batch_022.jsonl
+
+# 6. Batch-concatenation integrity:
+cat batches/batch_*.jsonl > /tmp/concat.jsonl && cmp /tmp/concat.jsonl kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl && echo CONCAT_OK
+
+# 7. JSON Schema validation of every record (optional, needs `pip install jsonschema`):
+python3 - <<'EOF'
+import json, jsonschema
+schema = json.load(open('schemas/record_schema.json'))
+recs = [json.loads(l) for l in open('kandoo_intent_dataset_v0.2.jsonl', encoding='utf-8') if l.strip()]
+[jsonschema.validate(r, schema) for r in recs]
+print('SCHEMA_OK', len(recs))
+EOF
+
+# 8. Manifest verification:
+sha256sum -c MANIFEST-SHA256.txt
+```
+
+> **Note on manifest vs re-runs:** `delivery_audit.py` embeds `executed_at_utc` timestamps in the 7 generated report files, so **re-running it legitimately changes those 7 hashes**. The manifest pins the *delivered snapshot*. Verify the manifest **before** re-running the audit (or expect exactly the 7 report files to differ afterwards: `qc_stage_a/b/c/d_report.json`, `dataset_statistics.json`, `human_review_priority.json`, `delivery_audit.json`).
+
+Requirements: Python ≥ 3.8, standard library only (check 7 additionally needs `jsonschema`).
